From 4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7f8091a2b3c4d5e6f70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 05:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] mmc: sdhci-cadence: program Host Control2 for eMMC too

sdhci_cdns_set_control_reg() calls sdhci_set_control_reg() only for SD cards.
That function sets the signal voltage and the UHS timing bits in Host
Control2, and eMMC needs the first of the two: a card in HS200 or HS400 runs
its I/O at 1.8 V, and SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180 is written nowhere else in the
driver.

The result on hardware is a bus that enumerates and then cannot move data. CMD
is a single line and tolerant enough to survive being driven at the wrong
level; the eight data lines are not. The AX630C shows it as an environment
read that reports "Transfer data timeout" and a filesystem read that reports
"fs_devread read error", with the card otherwise identified and its CSD read
correctly.

Call it unconditionally. For an eMMC still at 3.3 V nothing changes, because
the MMC_SIGNAL_VOLTAGE_330 arm of sdhci_set_voltage() is itself guarded by
IS_SD() and the UHS field is written from the selected mode either way.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -145,11 +145,14 @@
 	writel(tmp, plat->hrs_addr + SDHCI_CDNS_HRS06);
 
 	/*
-	 * For SD cards, program standard SDHCI Host Control2 UHS/voltage
-	 * registers for UHS-I support.
+	 * Program the standard SDHCI Host Control2 signal-voltage and UHS
+	 * timing bits. This is not SD-only: an eMMC in HS200 or HS400 runs its
+	 * I/O at 1.8 V, and SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180 is set nowhere else, so gating
+	 * this on IS_SD() leaves such a card being driven at 3.3 V. The bus
+	 * still enumerates -- CMD is one line and tolerant -- and then every
+	 * data transfer fails.
 	 */
-	if (IS_SD(mmc))
-		sdhci_set_control_reg(host);
+	sdhci_set_control_reg(host);
 
 	if (SDHCI_GET_VERSION(host) >= SDHCI_SPEC_420)
 		sdhci_cdns6_phy_adj(mmc->dev, plat, mmc->selected_mode);
